<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH SHELL CUTS DIESEL PRICE, GASOLINES UNCHANGED.</title>
<headline>DUTCH SHELL CUTS DIESEL PRICE, GASOLINES UNCHANGED.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit Shell Nederland BV said on Friday it will cut its retail price for diesel in the Netherlands by one cent per litre with effect from October 21.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices and the value of the dollar against the guilder, the company said. Gasoline prices will remain unchanged.</p>
<p>From Monday the price of diesel at Shell's self-service stations falls to 1.55 guilders per litre.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
